WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.650
Lab 2 compares the map with a real tenant.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.388
It's not run by the authors.

3
00:00:04.388 --> 00:00:07.045
Use a test tenant whose
groups are synchronized

4
00:00:07.045 --> 00:00:09.038
from a test domain, never production.

5
00:00:09.038 --> 00:00:13.488
You need PowerShell 7 with the Microsoft
Graph PowerShell S D K's groups module,

6
00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:17.529
an account that can consent to the
delegated group read all permission,

7
00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:21.912
and a groups file for your test domain's
groups, in the shape of the kit's fixture.

8
00:00:21.912 --> 00:00:23.763
Map your test groups with the kit.

9
00:00:23.763 --> 00:00:26.374
Sign in to Microsoft Graph, read-only.

10
00:00:26.374 --> 00:00:31.525
A Microsoft 365 G C C tenant uses
the worldwide Graph endpoint.

11
00:00:31.525 --> 00:00:35.916
List the tenant's groups with the properties
that decide the pattern, put the kit's

12
00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:40.175
answer beside what the tenant has, and
look for cloud groups that already exist.

13
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:42.363
Nothing in the lab writes to the tenant.

14
00:00:42.363 --> 00:00:46.390
To back it out, sign out of Graph
and delete the lab's output folder.
